MDL510, F15, F1, F12: mydumper merges the extra file into the defaults file
and reads the table sections from the merged file. When GLib rejects the
defaults file there is nothing to merge into: the extra file loads, but its
table section is ignored and users.email is dumped in plaintext. The defaults
file's [client] still provides the connection (the extra file has neither
[mydumper] nor [client], F14). mdl603-control-extra-file-without-tool-or-client-group
is the control: the same extra file masks the column when the defaults file
loads.
-- scenario --
tool: mydumper
versions: >= v0.19.1-1
args: --defaults-file /work/defaults.cnf --defaults-extra-file /work/extra.cnf --database app
lint: MDL110, MDL112, MDL405, MDL510
when < v0.19.3-1
# No pre-processor, hence no bracket state leak (MDL112).
lint: MDL110, MDL405, MDL510
end
expect config-loaded defaults.cnf: false
expect config-loaded extra.cnf: true
expect stderr-contains: Invalid key name
expect exit: 0
expect connected: true
expect column app.users.email: plaintext
when kb:table-sections-ignored
# F17: this mydumper loses every table section (MDL511).
lint: MDL110, MDL112, MDL405, MDL510, MDL511
end
-- defaults.cnf --
[client]
host=mysql
user=e2e
password=e2e-password

[mydumper]
key[bar baz]=1
-- extra.cnf --
[`app`.`users`]
`email`=random_string
-- .mydumper-lint.yaml --
load-sets:
  - defaults-file: defaults.cnf
    extra-files: [extra.cnf]
